# Wave W17-O (Route 113): sweep turf — ash-dulled grass under the permanent grey fall: a grey-green gone quiet, with paler SWEPT-CLEAN patches showing where the sweeper’s broom has lately passed and the ash flecks already settling back over them (design: calm speckled grass under a permanent fall of grey ash; the ash sweeper sweeps the road, the mountain unsweeps it). Route 113’s own ground — greyer and paler than Mt. Smokestack’s smoketurf (living summit grass with ash creeping at its edges): this grass lives UNDER the fall, swept and re-fallen, and split from Route 111’s hot olive failing grass by temperature — ash-grey, not dune-olive.
